WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.500
Good evening.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.234
Before we begin

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.102
with tonight's broadcast,

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.103
I want to say something about what

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.238
we witnessed at last night's town hall.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.573
Many of you have expressed

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.241
deep anger and disappointment.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.175
Many of you are upset

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.677
that someone who attempted to destroy

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.478
our democracy

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.045
was invited

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:12.979
to sit on the stage

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.581
in front of a crowd of Republican voters

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.016
to answer questions

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.317
and predictably continued

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.786
to spew lie after lie after lie

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.121
And I get it.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.889
It was disturbing.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.290
It was disturbing to see and hear

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:24.891
that person

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.192
refer to a black law enforcement

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.494
officers, a thug,

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.162
an adjective he used many times.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.430
Describe black men.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.097
And called Kaitlan

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.599
Collins, the moderator, nasty,

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.366
which is what he calls

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.934
any woman who stands up to him.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.903
It was disturbing to hear him

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.071
speak so highly of Q

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.806
and on conspirators and insurrection

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.041
is who assaulted

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:41.775
police officers

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.877
in our democracy on January six.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.345
And it was awful to hear him spread

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.647
ridiculous lies about the election.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.115
And it was certainly disturbing

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:49.582
to hear that

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.284
audience, young and old, our fellow

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.252
citizens, people

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.820
who love their kids and go to

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.222
church, laugh and applaud his lies

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.390
and his continued

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.625
defamation of a woman who,

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.060
according to a jury, of his peers,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.495
he's sexually abused and defamed

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.464
as good a job as Kaitlan Collins did,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.498
trying to fact check him.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.534
It is impossible to fact check fully

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:10.070
because he lies so shamelessly

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.838
Now, many of you think CNN shouldn't

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.740
have given him any platform to speak.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.542
And I understand the anger about that,

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.277
giving him the audience the time.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.711
I get that.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.880
But this is what I also get.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.215
The man you were so disturbed

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.983
to see and hear from last night,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.518
that man is the frontrunner

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.853
for the Republican nomination

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.021
for president.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:28.922
And according to polling

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.057
no other Republican is even close.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.325
That man

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.226
you were so upset

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.461
to hear from last night.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.162
He may be president of the United States

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.764
in less than two years.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.933
And that audience that upset you,

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:40.700
that's a sampling

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.635
of about half the country.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.903
They are your family

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.171
members, your neighbors,

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.639
and they are voting.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.075
And many said they're voting for him.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.243
Now, maybe

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.478
you haven't been paying attention to him

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.445
since he left office.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.580
And have you been enjoying

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.581
not hearing from him,

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.616
thinking it can happen again?

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.085
Some investigation is going to stop him?

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.020
Well, it hasn't so far.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.655
So if last night showed anything,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.824
it showed it can happen again.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:07.127
It is happening again.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.963
He hasn't changed and he is running hard.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.232
You have every right to be outraged today

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:12.699
and angry.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.701
Never watch this network again.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.503
But do you think staying in your silo

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.904
and only listening to people

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:18.538
you agree with

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.807
is going to make that person go away?

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.942
If we all only listen to those

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:23.843
we agree with,

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.312
it may actually do the opposite.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.148
If lives are allowed to go unchecked,

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.850
as imperfect as our ability to check them

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.886
is on a stage in real time,

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.554
those lies continue

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.256
and those lies spread.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:38.791
If you're angry or upset, I understand,

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.260
but you have the power

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.361
to do something about it.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.496
You can actually get involved.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.731
You can make a difference.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:47.033
Whatever side of the aisle you're on

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.302
after last night none of us can say,

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:51.504
I didn't know what's out there.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.940
I didn't know what's coming.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.141
We asked Republican senators

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.409
for their thoughts about last night.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:57.777
Some prefer not to say anything

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:58.344
others did.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.679
Here's a sampling of what we heard.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.882
What was the reason for

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.051
not supporting him? Where do I begin?

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:08.655
President Trump's judgment is, is wrong

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.722
in this case.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.090
President Putin

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.159
and his government have engaged

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.394
in war crimes.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.129
I think people saw last night

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.030
what they would get with

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.631
another term of

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.133
Donald Trump as president,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.135
which is completely untethered

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.269
to the truth.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.038
Uncertain as to whether he wants Russia

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.773
or Ukraine to win.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:27.840
And they

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.741
a brutal conflict

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.476
which Russia has imposed on Ukraine.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:30.910
You're asking me,

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:31.444
do I think you should

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.011
pardon people

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.080
who engage in rioting behavior?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.714
No, I don't.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.683
Anybody who crossed in

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:39.619
to the end of the capital

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:40.820
under the circumstances

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.422
that I witnessed firsthand,

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:43.389
it's hard for me to have

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:46.526
a positive predisposition towards them

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:47.527
more now from Jessica.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:48.761
And she's had the capital for us.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:48.962
And I.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:49.929
What more are you hearing

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.030
tonight, Jessica?

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.198
Well, let's start first

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.900
with the Republicans, both in the Senate

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.400
and the House.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:54.867
You just heard

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.169
from some Senate Republicans

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:56.803
there, Anderson.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:59.138
And people like Senator Mitt Romney.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.039
And that's somebody

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.741
who has been pretty outspoken

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.476
against former President Donald Trump.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.210
But it was somewhat

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.411
surprising to see somebody

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:05.945
like Senator

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.213
Josh Hawley

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.148
push back against some of his positions

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.450
that he took last night.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.918
And what we heard again and again

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.087
in talking with these Republican members

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.722
who who pushed back against

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.490
and had very different opinions

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.524
than former President Trump,

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.859
it really kind of circled around

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:20.760
three issues.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.696
It was Ukraine and Vladimir Putin.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.732
And if he is a war criminal or not

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.000
and who should win that war?

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.201
It was January 6th

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.670
and former President Trump's

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.139
pledge to perhaps pardon

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.041
people who were here at the Capitol

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:35.875
as insurrectionists

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:36.843
who have been convicted

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.111
and are serving time.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:38.911
And then it was also,

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:39.245
of course,

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:39.846
the debt ceiling,

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:40.246
which is what

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.148
looms very heavy here right now

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.116
as they work toward that

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.250
June 1st deadline

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.220
and allowing the nation to default.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.322
Those were really the key issues.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.090
We also heard similar things

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.225
from members of the House

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.226
GOP who kind of

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.094
came back to those same issues as well.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.362
But, Anderson,

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.631
even in hearing some of these Republicans

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.799
speaking out against the former

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:00.566
president, that's

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.368
that's still just a handful of people.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.670
And let's be very clear,

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.972
he still has an enormous amount of power

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.107
and an enormous support system

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.510
here among Republicans on Capitol Hill.

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.445
And what about reaction from Democrats?

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:12.679
Well,

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:14.414
as you can imagine, Democrats

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:15.415
have never been fans

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:16.649
of the former president.

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.017
And that certainly continued.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.052
And what we saw

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.053
was the Democratic Party

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.621
really trying to attach

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:22.388
Donald Trump,

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.623
the MAGA,

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:24.624
MAGA Republicans,

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.526
which has really been their line

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.760
that they have

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.261
that President

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.562
Biden has used as well,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.230
to kind of put them all together

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.599
as a party that is too extreme to lead.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.168
And that is the case that we heard

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:35.635
the making

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.270
we heard the Senate majority

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.304
leader, Chuck Schumer,

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.739
talking about how bad

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:41.174
President Trump has, what he called

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:43.209
enormous sway over House Speaker

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.043
Kevin McCarthy

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.578
as he navigates these debt

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.313
ceiling negotiations.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.214
We heard from Hakeem

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.850
Jeffries, who leads the House Democrats,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.885
and he said that this was exhibit A

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:55.021
of the trauma that America would see

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.056
if we have another four years

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:58.191
with President Trump.

00:05:58.191 --> 00:05:59.125
And then we also heard

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:00.159
from Richard Blumenthal,

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:01.260
the senator from Connecticut,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.296
who said that if he were to pardon

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:04.797
those January 6th

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:05.631
rioters, that

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.266
that would be grounds for yet

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.102
another impeachment in his eyes.

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:09.869
So, again,

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.371
a lot from the Democrats

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.805
that you would expect

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.240
really trying to stake their positions

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.541
make it very clear

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.843
that they are quite different

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:18.244
than the Democrats offer,

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:20.380
a very, very, very different view

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.214
than Donald Trump

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:22.882
and attaching him to that far right

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.617
wing of the party

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.085
Also interesting, Anderson,

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.019
just to go back to the

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.788
to the Senate Republicans for one second.

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:31.224
We did talk to the Senate majority whip,

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:33.192
John Thune, who said it

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.560
looks like a lot of Democrat

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.629
campaign ads were written last night.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:37.864
I'm just kidding.

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:38.331
Appreciate it.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:39.232
Want to get some perspective

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:39.665
now with me

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:40.266
here, Republican

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:42.068
consultant and CNN political commentator

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.002
Margaret Hoover,

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:44.470
host of Firing Line on PBS

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:45.505
also Anthony Scaramucci,

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:46.506
who briefly served as White House

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:47.373
communications director

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.541
to the former president

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:49.275
and our own chief

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:50.243
White House correspondent,

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.210
Phil Mattingly.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:51.577
Anthony,

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:52.578
do you think anything has happened

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:52.845
in the past

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:55.248
24 hours that have changed the dynamics

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:57.750
for this GOP primary race?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.651
Not yet,

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:00.520
but I think you guys are bringing up

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.021
something that could change it.

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:05.258
And that is an onslaught of senators

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:07.226
and House of Representative

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.728
congressional leaders

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.129
going against the president.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.964
I think that would be a snowball

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.833
rolling in a direction

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:15.168
that he actually couldn't stop.

00:07:15.168 --> 00:07:17.336
And so they're still fearing him

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.571
because he's a big bully

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:19.806
and their political consultants

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:20.673
are telling them,

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:21.908
don't say anything about them

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:22.942
or don't make a comment.

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.911
But if they start to stand up to him

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.078
the way Mitt Romney did,

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:26.946
he saw a glimmer of

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:28.848
that was Senator Hawley.

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:30.149
You will blunt him.

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:31.517
You will slow him down.

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:32.452
And remember

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:33.553
when the witch

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:34.487
and the Wizard of Oz,

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:35.087
the water

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:36.923
accidentally spilled on the witch

00:07:36.923 --> 00:07:39.358
and she started melting,

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.426
the soldiers turned it.

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.360
Dorothy said, hey, geez,

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.363
I'm sorry that we did this and I think

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:46.098
we're getting to that point right now

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:48.134
where the water has to hit Trump

00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:49.735
and he has to start melting

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:50.403
and they have to show

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.038
some bravery and courage.

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:53.306
There's a lot of munchkins on Capitol

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:53.639
Hill, though.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:54.273
I mean,

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.175
are they are they really ready to support

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:56.476
the House

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:57.743
of Representatives in the Senate?

